WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.849
Start a new fabric costing.

2
00:00:04.089 --> 00:00:05.369
Name the fabric,

3
00:00:05.489 --> 00:00:07.687
enter its warp and weft construction,

4
00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.475
and include the crimp and waste allowances.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.235
Add the warp yarn’s denier, beam ends, rate and
G S T.

6
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:25.613
These inputs determine warp consumption and
cost.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.149
Enter the weft yarn, picks per inch, fabric
width, denier, rate and G S T.

8
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.255
Review the weaving cost and overhead.

9
00:00:48.495 --> 00:00:51.687
Then enter your target margin and order
quantity.

10
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.363
Open Live Cost to see your estimate.

11
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.792
Review the pricing assumptions,

12
00:01:06.912 --> 00:01:11.041
then return to the inputs to explore a different
costing scenario.

13
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.318
Increase the weft rate to one hundred and twenty
eight rupees per kilogram,

14
00:01:19.438 --> 00:01:21.725
and set the margin to fifteen percent.

15
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.617
Live Cost now shows the updated production cost
and selling price.

16
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.081
Switch to Detailed to inspect the yarn
calculations, including consumption, crimp and
waste.

17
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.256
Scroll down to review the production cost
breakdown.

18
00:01:49.496 --> 00:01:54.711
Quick and Detailed use the same calculations,
with different levels of detail.
